{"event": "model_request", "time": 1793846976.0357676, "run_id": "948a987e83be45cba9d83d4b512e1695", "seq": 5, "number": 1, "body": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Complete the task using the Python tools below.\nReturn ONE JSON object with string fields \"thought\" (next action) and \"code\" (executable Python), then STOP.\nExample: {\"thought\":\"Check progress.\",\"code\":\"print(task_status())\"}\nNo Markdown fences, extra JSON, simulated observations or future turns. Keep the action within the output budget.\n\nCall tools with keyword arguments; arrays are Python lists. Print needed output. Variables and imports persist,\nand successful statements before an error remain executed. Paths are relative to the task repository.\nUse tools for all file/command operations; edit only allowed files, never tests. Use current file_hash as expected_hash.\nImports allowed: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']; import before use. Read sufficient evidence and avoid repeated unchanged reads.\nWhen the business deliverable is ready, call final_answer: it runs missing current-version verification,\ncompletes the plan on success, or returns the failure for repair. It cannot supply missing reading, baseline or report.\n\nAvailable tools:\n```python\ndef list_files(path: str = None, limit: int = None, offset: int = None) -> dict:\n    'List text files under a repository path.\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nlimit: {\"type\":\"integer\"}\\noffset: {\"type\":\"integer\"}'\n\ndef search_code(query: str, paths: list = None, limit: int = None) -> dict:\n    'Search visible text source files for a literal string.\\nquery: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\npaths: {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}\\nlimit: {\"type\":\"integer\"}'\n\ndef read_file(path: str) -> dict:\n    'Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result[\\'content\\'], not result[:N].\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef read_range(path: str, start_line: int, end_line: int) -> dict:\n    'Read an inclusive line range from a text file. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nstart_line: {\"type\":\"integer\"}\\nend_line: {\"type\":\"integer\"}'\n\ndef read_symbol(path: str, symbol: str) -> dict:\n    'Read a complete Python class or function including decorators. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nsymbol: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef write_file(path: str, content: str, expected_hash: str) -> dict:\n    'Replace an editable text file after checking its current hash.\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\ncontent: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nexpected_hash: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef replace_text_batch(path: str, edits: list, expected_hash: str) -> dict:\n    'Atomically replace unique nonoverlapping occurrences from one file version. Returns ok, path, before_hash, file_hash, changed.\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nedits: {\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"Python list of objects, e.g. [{\\'old_text\\':\\'before\\',\\'new_text\\':\\'after\\'}]; all refer to the original file.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"old_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"new_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"old_text\",\"new_text\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}\\nexpected_hash: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef run_command(argv: list, cwd: str = None) -> dict:\n    'Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use \\'.\\' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\\nargv: {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}\\ncwd: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef update_plan(items: list) -> dict:\n    'Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\\nitems: {\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"List of objects, e.g. [{\\\\\"title\\\\\":\\\\\"Read sources\\\\\",\\\\\"status\\\\\":\\\\\"doing\\\\\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\"}'\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: list) -> dict:\n    'Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\\nevidence_ids: {\"type\":\"array\"}'\n\ndef task_status() -> dict:\n    'Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.'\n\ndef write_note(title: str, content: str, evidence_ids: list, section: str = None) -> dict:\n    'Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence. Returns dict: note_id, sources, chars.\\ntitle: {\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\"}\\ncontent: {\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"One contiguous string literal, 20..3000 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\"}\\nevidence_ids: {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Python list[str], e.g. [\\'ev-abc\\'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\"}\\nsection: {\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional stable note key; source notes still allow 20..3000 characters.\"}'\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nFix calc.py and verify.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"source\", \"editable\": [\"calc.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 6}\nUse update_plan before editing and run baseline checks. os and pathlib are unavailable in action code.\nFor write_note, put the complete exact note text in thought and pass the same text as one content string literal in code.\nRead all three files with read_file first, then read/reuse complete mechanisms from all three\nbefore the first edit. Source notes are OPTIONAL; current source blocks can be used directly.\nWhen progress says phase=edit, the initial reading and baseline are satisfied. Apply a scoped edit and verify.\nA note may replace original text only after its mechanisms were exposed. Do not repeat full reads to register them again.\n\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"baseline\",\"next_requirement\":\"baseline: python -m pytest -q\",\"remaining_count\":4,\"requests_left\":5,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":1,\"max_requests\":6,\"requests_after_response\":5,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"full_reads_registered\":{},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"required_mechanisms_exposed\":{}}"}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"]}, "chars": 7059, "content_chars": 6448, "course_content_chars": 6888}
